  "kind": "definition",
  "title": "Standard graded algebras",
  "statement": "Let $k$ be a field. A standard graded $k$-algebra is a commutative\n$k$-algebra with a direct-sum decomposition $S=\\bigoplus_{n\\ge0}S_n$\nsuch that $S_0=k$, $S_aS_b\\subseteq S_{a+b}$, and $S$ is generated\nas a $k$-algebra by finitely many elements of $S_1$.\nAn element of $S_n$ is homogeneous of degree $n$.\nAn ideal $I$ is homogeneous if every homogeneous component of each\nof its elements is again in $I$. The ideal\n$S_+=\\bigoplus_{n>0}S_n$ is called the irrelevant ideal.\nFor a homogeneous element $f$, write $S_{(f)}$ for the degree-zero\nsubring of the graded localization $S[f^{-1}]$.",
